    "Question #: 1": {
      "Title": "Exam 1z0-580 topic 1 question 1 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "What information would the \"beadm list -ds\" command output?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. a list of all Bes"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. a list of the datasets and snapshot information for the active BE"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. a list of the datasets and snapshot information for all Bes"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. a list of the default sets"
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. a list of BEs in machine readable format"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: C \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You can display information about snapshots, boot environments, and datasets that were created by the beadm command by using the beadm list subcommand."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The beadm list command output also displays boot environments that are created by the pkg command."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The beadm list command syntax is:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Syntax: beadm list [-a | [-ds] [-H] [BeName]"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The command lists information about the existing boot environment. To view information for a specific boot environment, replace BeName with a boot environment name. If a specific boot environment is not specified, the command lists information about all boot environments. The default is to list boot environments without additional information."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "-a Lists all available information about the boot environment. This information includes subordinate datasets and snapshots."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "-d Lists information about all subordinate datasets that belong to the boot environment."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "-s Lists information about the snapshots of the boot environment."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "-H Prevents listing header information. Each field in the output is separated by a semicolon."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Reference: Oracle Solaris 11 Information Library, Listing Existing Boot Environments and Snapshots"
          }
        ]
      },
