    "Question #: 2": {
      "Title": "Exam 1z0-580 topic 1 question 13 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which two statements are true of the GRUB menu?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. GRUB is the default boot loader for Oracle Solaris 11 SPARC and x86."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. GRUB supports Oracle Solaris and Oracle Linux only."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. GRUB loads a kernel based upon the file name, disk, and partition specified."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. GRUB uses boot environments for all operating systems."
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. GRUB is fully compliant with the Multiboot specification."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: AC \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "* If your system has more than one OS installed on the system or more than one root boot environment in a ZFS root pool, you can boot from these boot environments for both SPARC and x86 platforms."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "* GRUB, the open source boot loader, is the default boot loader in the Solaris OS."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "C: With GRUB based booting, the kernel is loaded by specifying its file name, and the drive, and the partition where the kernel resides. GRUB based booting replaces the Solaris Device Configuration Assistant and simplifies the booting process with a GRUB menu."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Incorrect:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Not E:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "* In this implementation of GRUB, the multiboot module is no longer used."
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A:"
